I can't believe that you let the game go so bad once you had seen a
magic whistle.
It is the single most important weapon that you will need as a healer.

You could have done the following.

The healer starts with a lot of money. So you could have simply
bought all the three things at once and moved everything in the shop
in a single heap at the corner of the shop, and then adding something
cursed at the top.

Then you could have dropped the money to the floor that would suffice
for the three things. Then you could have paid. After that you could
have
waited for your pet to pick up the money from the ground while standing

on the door, and then applied the whistle, repeatedly till the pet was
outside the shop.

Trap doors are very frustrating, but if you have already found a
whistle
it may be useful to dive into the trap door after your pet. There is a
chance
that you both end up on the same level, or else you get to search for
your
pet using Elbereth.

Ofcourse Elbereth is not very reliable but being a healer even at XL1
you
should have decent HP to survive quite a few turns unless you are
surrounded.
But surrounding does not happen in One Turn. You should start writing
Elbereth
as soon as you can.

Also always level up to 3-4 so that you can cast stone to flesh, and
collect
some stones to make meatballs, for use as charming granades.

healers are actually not that difficult once you get a nice army of
pets. You should
be able to finish the mines end with there help without any need for a
polymorph trap.
And boulders make it trivial to survive very long in the dungeon and
there is no
pressing need to find more food.

